# ==============================================================================
# The Business Cut LMS — Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================
#
# NOTE: The application operates fully out of the box in Demo Mode without
# requiring any environment variables or external database keys.
#
# If TMDB_API_KEY is not set, the LMS uses high-fidelity cinematic SVG/editorial
# placeholder posters and verified offline movie metadata.

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. The Movie Database (TMDB) API Configuration
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required ONLY if you wish to fetch live movie posters and metadata from TMDB.
#
# How to obtain a TMDB API key:
# 1. Sign up for a free account at https://www.themoviedb.org/signup
# 2. Go to your Account Settings -> API (https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api)
# 3. Request an API Key (Developer / Educational use)
# 4. Copy the "API Key (v3 auth)" and paste it below.
#
# SECURITY NOTE:
# This key is strictly accessed by Next.js server-side route handlers (src/app/api/tmdb/route.ts).
# It is NEVER exposed to the client-side JavaScript bundle.
TMDB_API_KEY=your_tmdb_api_key_v3_here

# Optional: TMDB Read Access Token (v4 auth Bearer token) if preferred
# TMDB_READ_ACCESS_TOKEN=your_tmdb_v4_read_access_token_here

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. Application & Vercel Deployment Settings
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME="The Business Cut"
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Production Persistence & Authentication (Future Extensibility)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# By default, "The Business Cut" uses client-side localStorage persistence for
# the prototype and demo mode. To connect an external PostgreSQL / Supabase
# database or NextAuth in production:
#
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/business_cut_lms?schema=public"
# NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
# NEXTAUTH_SECRET="generate-a-strong-secret-with-openssl-rand-base64-32"
